  },
  {
    "sheet": "xl/worksheets/sheet1.xml",
    "cell": "E51",
    "value": "These accounts are the minimum requirements for the company to be compliant with its filing obligations under s29 of the ITA 2010.  Companies may exceed this minimum filing requirement."
  },
  {
    "sheet": "xl/worksheets/sheet1.xml",
    "cell": "E53",
    "value": "(i)"
  },
  {
    "sheet": "xl/worksheets/sheet1.xml",
    "cell": "F53",
    "value": "A company which is in the process of being liquidated and has assessable income in Gibraltar is required to comply with the minimum accounts filing requirements stated above plus a detailed tax computation plus full settlement of the tax liability on the filing date;"
  },
  {
    "sheet": "xl/worksheets/sheet1.xml",
    "cell": "E54",
    "value": "A company which is pending being struck off the Register (under the Companies Act 2014) is required to make a full and complete return until such time as it is struck off and thereby dissolved.  In the event that a company which has previously been struck off should be reinstated on the Register, its filing obligations in accordance with s29 of the Income Tax Act 2010 will apply as per the table above."
  },
  {
    "sheet": "xl/worksheets/sheet1.xml",
    "cell": "E56",
    "value": "An incomplete return will incur penalties under section 65 of the ITA 2010."
